<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11741"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 3:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Those girls disappeared from the San Francisco Bay Area in the late 1980s and early 1990s. Timothy Bindner, a University of California Berkeley graduate was a suspect in the abduction of the girls and possibly many more. Bindner was obsessed with visiting the graves of young girls. He visited the grave of Angela Bugay hundreds of times. The Harvard educated psychologist, John Philpin wrote Stalemate: A Shocking True Story of Child Abduction and Murder. It an attempts to explain the disappearances and provides an insight into the mind of Bindner.  <BR> <BR>I have an interest in the abduction of Nyleen Kay Marshall. She was abducted from the Helena National Forest in the Elkhorn Mountains, Montana in June 1983 at four years of age. The abductor corresponded with the police in 1986 and made several telephone calls to a New York child find network. Its believed the abductor lives in Wisconsin and Nyleen Kay Marshall is alive and possibly unaware that her family has been searching for her for almost 22 years. She will be 27 years old in September. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
