<!--Post: 12240--><!--Time: 1111792139-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12240"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 3:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->weeza, i think they took the poor childs pic for a reason, also have another idea about why the police could not find evidence of the girls clothes etc. Remember the last earthquake, digging for survivors, good place to bury evidence.  today is My Birthday, I am alive, I am putting all the victims on my WatchDogg, for LE site, please add all you can for the children. <a href="Http://www.geocities.com/embersage2003" target=_top>Http://www.geocities.com/embersage2003</a> <BR>Love Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
