<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12241"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 3:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Timothy Bindner, the prime suspect in the disappearance of several girls in the San Francisco Bay area has suggested a possible murder theory. He believes the abductor murdered the girls and placed the corpses in graves underneath coffins being prepared for funerals the next day. Bindner was employed as a gravedigger among other menial occupations he held over the years. He is a suspected serial murderer, but law enforcement has never been able to gather sufficient evidence to apprehend him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
