<!--Post: 12286--><!--Time: 1111875141-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12286"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 26, 2005 - 2:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A portrait of Timothy Bindner can be found below: <BR> <BR>Name: Timothy James Bindner <BR>Date of Birth: February 26 1948 <BR>Place of Birth: Hammond, Indiana <BR>High School: Graduated from Pacific High School, California in 1966 <BR>College: Studied forestry at the University of California Riverside. Left after becoming dissatisfied with the curriculum. He transferred to the University of Idaho, but left after arriving. Began studying forestry at the University of California Berkeley in September. He graduated from Berkeley with a cumulative grade-point average of 3.62. <BR>Marital Status: Married Terry, his high school girlfriend on September 7 1968. The marriage was dissolved in 1979. Bindner married Sandra Wilson in June 1988. They married a day after the disappearance of Amber Swartz. <BR>Occupations: Bindner was employed at the Portland Water Company in September 1972. He was also employed at a local McDonald&#39;s restaurant. He and Terry returned to Southern California in 1973. He began employment at the Social Security Administration in Richmond near San Francisco in 1975. He was dismissed from the Social Security Administration in 1985 for sending gifts and cards to teenaged girls. He obtained their names, addresses and ages from confidential computer files. His actions were not illegal and he was reinstated for sixteen months. He was employed at the Social Security Administration when Swartz disappeared.    <BR>Family: Bindner&#39;s father was a lieutenant colonel in the army with twenty years experience. He spent most of his time in the Signal Corps. He developed radio communications. His mother was a nurse during the Second World War. He has three brothers and a sister.  <BR> <BR>Bibliography <BR> <BR>Philpin, J. &#40;1997&#41;, Stalemate: A Shocking True Story of Child Abduction and Murder, Bantam Books, New York<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12286-->
<!--Post: 12292--><!--Time: 1111883445-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12292"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 26, 2005 - 4:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yeah ok, This guy had access to peoples personal information Creepy, Thank you for the Bio information, I will be very helpful. Thanks E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
